From 2403b0c62fda8dd4197eee1938206b01e4654c07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kgoncalv <kayo.goncalvesdacosta@windriver.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:41:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Reconcile stale kernel-OVS provider bridge ports

The auto_bridge_add handling in the neutron-ovs-agent init
script only ever calls add-br/add-port for the current
desired bridge mapping. If a datanetwork is unassigned from
a data interface (or the interface is deleted or reclassed),
its entry disappears from auto_bridge_add on the next
render, but the physical port already added to the br-phy*
bridge is never removed. The stale port stays attached to
the bridge indefinitely, and stx-openstack has no other
mechanism to clean it up.

Add a reconciliation pass right after the existing
add-br/add-port loop: recompute the desired {bridge: iface}
mapping from the same auto_bridge_add source, then for
every br-phy* bridge remove any non-patch port that does
not match what is expected there. This never adds a port,
only the existing loop does that, and it never touches
br-int/br-tun or any patch port (phy-*/int-*), only the
kernel-OVS provider bridges themselves.

Skipped entirely when DPDK_ENABLED is true, since DPDK
bridges are already managed declaratively via sysinv's
puppet (platform::vswitch::ovs), which reconciles ports on
every config-apply independent of this script.

Since interface-datanetwork assignment changes require the
owning host to be locked first, this reconciliation always
runs on the same unlock cycle that made the change possible
in the first place, so the stale port is cleaned up as soon
as the pod is recreated with the corrected mapping.

Signed-off-by: kgoncalv <kayo.goncalvesdacosta@windriver.com>
---
 .../_neutron-openvswitch-agent-init.sh.tpl    | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/neutron/templates/bin/_neutron-openvswitch-agent-init.sh.tpl b/neutron/templates/bin/_neutron-openvswitch-agent-init.sh.tpl
index 72c14d882..f9d147ee3 100644
--- a/neutron/templates/bin/_neutron-openvswitch-agent-init.sh.tpl
+++ b/neutron/templates/bin/_neutron-openvswitch-agent-init.sh.tpl
@@ -506,6 +506,31 @@ do
   fi
 done
 
+# Remove stale ports from kernel-OVS provider bridges. The loop above only
+# ever adds ports; if a datanetwork is unassigned from a data interface,
+# the stale physical port is otherwise left attached to its br-phy* bridge
+# indefinitely. DPDK bridges are excluded: they are managed declaratively
+# via puppet (platform::vswitch::ovs), which already reconciles ports
+# on every config-apply.
+if [[ "${DPDK_ENABLED}" != "true" ]]; then
+  declare -A desired_bridge_map
+  for bmap in `sed 's/[{}"]//g' /tmp/auto_bridge_add | tr "," "\n"`
+  do
+    bridge=${bmap%:*}
+    iface=${bmap#*:}
+    desired_bridge_map["$bridge"]=$iface
+  done
+  for bridge in $(ovs-vsctl --db=unix:${OVS_SOCKET} list-br 2>/dev/null | grep "^br-phy"); do
+    expected="${desired_bridge_map[$bridge]:-}"
+    for existing in $(ovs-vsctl --db=unix:${OVS_SOCKET} list-ports "$bridge" 2>/dev/null); do
+      case "$existing" in phy-*|int-*) continue ;; esac
+      if [ "$existing" != "$expected" ]; then
+        ovs-vsctl --db=unix:${OVS_SOCKET} --if-exists del-port "$bridge" "$existing"
+      fi
+    done
+  done
+fi
+
 tunnel_types="{{- .Values.conf.plugins.openvswitch_agent.agent.tunnel_types -}}"
 if [[ -n "${tunnel_types}" ]] ; then
     tunnel_interface="{{- .Values.network.interface.tunnel -}}"
